 247:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** Where:
 248:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** 'destination_address' (DA): the address of the device(s) intended
 249:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** to receive the service primitive. Its format (device name,
 250:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** network address, etc.) is a local matter. This address may
 251:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** also be a multicast, local broadcast or global broadcast type.
 252:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** 'source_address' (SA): the address of the device from which
 253:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** the service primitive was received. Its format (device name,
 254:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** network address, etc.) is a local matter.
 255:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** 'network_priority' (NP): a four-level network priority parameter
 256:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** described in 6.2.2.
 257:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** 'data_expecting_reply' (DER): a Boolean parameter that indicates
 258:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** whether (TRUE) or not (FALSE) a reply service primitive
 259:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** is expected for the service being issued.
 260:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** */
