 288:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c **** /** Decode the NPDU portion of a received message, particularly the NCPI byte.
 289:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *  The Network Layer Protocol Control Information byte is described
 290:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *  in section 6.2.2 of the BACnet standard.
 291:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  * @param npdu [in] Buffer holding the received NPDU header bytes (must be at least 2)
 292:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  * @param dest [out] Returned with routing destination information if the NPDU
 293:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *                   has any and if this points to non-null storage for it.
 294:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *                   If dest->net and dest->len are 0 on return, there is no
 295:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *                   routing destination information.
 296:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  * @param src  [out] Returned with routing source information if the NPDU
 297:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *                   has any and if this points to non-null storage for it.
 298:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *                   If src->net and src->len are 0 on return, there is no
 299:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *                   routing source information.
 300:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *                   This src describes the original source of the message when
 301:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *                   it had to be routed to reach this BACnet Device.
 302:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  * @param npdu_data [out] Returns a filled-out structure with information
 303:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  * 					 decoded from the NCPI and other NPDU bytes.
 304:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  * @return On success, returns the number of bytes which were decoded from the
 305:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  * 		   NPDU section; if this is a  network layer message, there may be more
 306:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *         bytes left in the NPDU; if not a network msg, the APDU follows.
 307:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  *         If 0 or negative, there were problems with the data or arguments.
 308:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/npdu.c ****  */
